{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For [they shall be ashamed] of the terebinths. </b> From the root אלה (Genesis 18:6), joined with the masculine plural sign, like נשים, also שלש סאים, and the proof is from the Gaon [Saadia]." "Some say that the yod of <b>יֵבֹשׁוּ </b>is in place of the second-person tav [i.e., תֵּבֹשׁוּ], and there are many like it. In my opinion, it is joined with יָכְלוּ, and afterward it returns to speak to the second person, and there are many like it." "<b>And you shall be confounded. </b> Like תֵּבֹשׁוּ."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Saadia's reading; 'the proof is from the Gaon' likely refers to Saadia's grammatical interpretation confirming this derivation.", 1 "The argument concerns whether יֵבֹשׁוּ is third person or a second-person form with yod replacing tav; 'joined with יכלו' apparently refers to an adjacent verse or syntactic unit."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:36.931528953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}